# Secrets — never commit keys. This file must exist in the FIRST commit.
.env
.env.*
*.key
*_API_KEY*

# Raw API responses (regenerable; may be large) — covers results/, results_haiku/, any future per-model dirs
results*/raw/
# v1.2 (r4): a rerun moves the previous outputs, raw/ included, to <out>/_previous/<UTC>/.
# Keep the archived raw responses private as well (review P06-ED F02).
results*/_previous/
**/_previous/**/raw/

# Python
__pycache__/
*.pyc
.venv/

# OS/editor
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db

# Real-world artifacts — NEVER commit or publish (employer data, internal identifiers)
data_private/

# Arm B private mapping — abstract document IDs to real photo filenames, per-document months
# and the writer's own encodings. Filenames, encodings and the month of each document appear
# only here; the pre-registrations name the documents' overall date range and one month.
# Never commit, never publish.
# Anchoring corrected 2026-09-12: the patterns below were ROOT-anchored, so they protected
# kit-B/ only if it landed at the repository root. The probe kit actually lives at
# ed-eval-probe/kit-B/, which the root-anchored forms did NOT cover. Every rule is now
# depth-independent. A gitignore keeps files out of commits; it is not access control (see
# docs/PROBE-AMENDMENT-01.md section 4b). It must at least cover the paths the code really writes.
**/private-map.json
**/kit-B/*.gold.json
**/kit-B/intent_*.csv
**/probe-run/
**/probe_b_results/
**/probe_results/raw/
**/photos/
results*/raw/

# Local review and working files -- never commit (added 2026-09-25).
# .qa-review/ holds an external QA review, its virtualenv and generated artefacts; its own
# .gitignore covered only the venv and caches, so `git add -A` would have staged the review.
.qa-review/
venv/
# The Arm B intent workbook holds real months and legends once it is filled in.
**/*_FOUNDER*.docx

# Multi-model runs (r6): raw answers, attempt ledgers and run status. Regenerable from a recorded run;
# raw answers stay private like results*/raw/. Configuration (configs/) stays trackable.
mm_runs/
